ridden. The deployment begins building immediately and transitions through `QUEUED` → `INITIALIZING` → `BUILDING` before reaching `READY` or `ERROR`."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.deployments.deleteDeployment","description":"This API allows you to delete a deployment, either by supplying its `id` in the URL or the `url` of the deployment as a query parameter. You can obtain the ID, for example, by listing all deployments."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.deployments.getDeployment","description":"Retrieves information for a deployment either by supplying its ID (`id` property) or Hostname (`url` property). Additional details will be included when the authenticated user or team is an owner of the deployment."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.deployments.getDeploymentEvents","description":"Get the build logs of a deployment by deployment ID and build ID. It can work as an infinite stream of logs or as a JSON endpoint depending on the input parameters."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.deployments.getDeploymentFileContents","description":"Allows to retrieve the content of a file by supplying the file identifier and the deployment unique identifier. The response body will contain a JSON response containing the contents of the file encoded as base64."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.deployments.listDeploymentFiles","description":"Allows to retrieve the file structure of the source code of a deployment by supplying the deployment unique identifier. If the deployment was created with the Vercel CLI or the API directly with the `files` key, it will have a file tree that can be retrievable."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.marketplace.updateResourceSecretsById","description":"This endpoint updates the secrets of a resource. If a resource has projects connected, the connected secrets are updated with the new secrets. The old secrets may still be used by existing connected projects because they are not automatically redeployed. Redeployment is a manual action and must be completed by the user. All new project connections will use the new secrets.<br/> <br/> Use cases for this endpoint:<br/> <br/> - Resetting the credentials of a database in the partner. If the user requests the credentials to be updated in the partner’s application, the partner post the new set of secrets to Vercel, the user should redeploy their application and the expire the old credentials.<br/>"},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.projects.createProjectTransferRequest","description":"Initiates a project transfer request from one team to another. <br/> Returns a `code` that remains valid for 24 hours and can be used to accept the transfer request by another team using the `PUT /projects/transfer-request/:code` endpoint. <br/> Users can also accept the project transfer request using the claim URL: `https://vercel.com/claim-deployment?code=<code>&returnUrl=<returnUrl>`. <br/> The `code` parameter specifies the project transfer request code generated using this endpoint. <br/> The `returnUrl` parameter redirects users to a specific page of the application if the claim URL is invalid or expired."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.projects.pauseProject","description":"Pause a project by passing its project `id` in the URL. If the project does not exist given the id then the request will fail with 400 status code. If the project disables auto assigning custom production domains and blocks the active Production Deployment then the request will return with 200 status code."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.projects.unpauseProject","description":"Unpause a project by passing its project `id` in the URL. If the project does not exist given the id then the request will fail with 400 status code. If the project enables auto assigning custom production domains and unblocks the active Production Deployment then the request will return with 200 status code."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.user.listUserEvents","description":"Retrieves a list of "events" generated by the User on Vercel. Events are generated when the User performs a particular action, such as logging in, creating a deployment, and joining a Team (just to name a few). When the `teamId` parameter is supplied, then the events that are returned will be in relation to the Team that was specified."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.marketplace.updateResourceSecrets","description":"This endpoint is deprecated and replaced with the endpoint [Update Resource Secrets](#update-resource-secrets). <br/> This endpoint updates the secrets of a resource. If a resource has projects connected, the connected secrets are updated with the new secrets. The old secrets may still be used by existing connected projects because they are not automatically redeployed. Redeployment is a manual action and must be completed by the user. All new project connections will use the new secrets.<br/> <br/> Use cases for this endpoint:<br/> <br/> - Resetting the credentials of a database in the partner. If the user requests the credentials to be updated in the partner’s application, the partner post the new set of secrets to Vercel, the user should redeploy their application and the expire the old credentials.<br/>"}],[{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.deployments.listDeploymentFiles","description":"Allows to retrieve the file structure of the source code of a deployment by supplying the deployment unique identifier. If the deployment was created with the Vercel CLI or the API directly with the `files` key, it will have a file tree that can be retrievable."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.deployments.getDeployments","description":"List deployments under the authenticated user or team. If a deployment hasn't finished uploading (is incomplete), the `url` property will have a value of `null`."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.checksV2.listDeploymentCheckRuns","description":"List all check runs for a deployment."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.aliases.listDeploymentAliases","description":"Retrieves all Aliases for the Deployment with the given ID. The authenticated user or team must own the deployment."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.deployments.deleteDeployment","description":"This API allows you to delete a deployment, either by supplying its `id` in the URL or the `url` of the deployment as a query parameter. You can obtain the ID, for example, by listing all deployments."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.user.listUserEvents","description":"Retrieves a list of "events" generated by the User on Vercel. Events are generated when the User performs a particular action, such as logging in, creating a deployment, and joining a Team (just to name a few). When the `teamId` parameter is supplied, then the events that are returned will be in relation to the Team that was specified."},{"path":"vercel_api.user.personalvercelapi.checks.getAllChecks","description":"List all of the checks created for a deployment."}]],"logs":[]}}

